  "final_message": "I built the account service, lockout, per-client limit, admin unlock and frontend. I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't installed here. I ran the backend under gunicorn and checked it with Flask's test client and curl, and the frontend type-checks and builds.\n\nWhat I confirmed when running it:\n- **Accounts:** register answers 201; a second registration with the same name in different case answers 409. Login returns a token, and `/api/me` answers 401 without one.\n- **Lockout:** five wrong passwords give 401 each. The sixth attempt, even with the right password, gets 429 with `Retry-After: 900`.\n- **Admin:** `/api/admin/locks` lists the locked name, and a non-admin gets 403. After the admin unlocks it, the right password signs in again.\n- **Per-client limit:** the 21st attempt in a minute from one client gets 429 with `Retry-After: 59`. A different client address is not blocked.\n- **Restart:** after restarting without `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, the lock was still in place and admin sign-in was refused.\n\nA few behaviours you might not expect:\n- **Unknown usernames can be locked too.** Failures count by name, and a lock appears in the admin list even if no account has that name.\n- **Usernames ignore case.** `Alice` and `alice` are the same account and share one lock.\n- **The per-client limit uses fixed minutes.** The minute starts at the client's first attempt, and refusals until it ends still count as attempts. \"Client\" means the connecting IP address. Behind a reverse proxy, set `TRUST_PROXY=1` to use `X-Forwarded-For` instead; only do that if the proxy is trusted.\n- **Admin password changes sign the admin out.** It's set again from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` at each start, and changing or removing it ends the admin's existing sessions.\n- **Additions beyond the spec:**\n  - `POST /api/auth/logout`, used by the sign-out button.\n  - `is_admin` in `/api/me`.\n  - A `reason` on each sign-in attempt (whether it failed because of the lock).\n  - Extra fields in 429 responses (`code`, `retry_after`, `retry_at`), which the form uses to say which limit applied and when to try again.\n- **Registration rules:** usernames must be 3\u201364 characters (letters, digits, `_ . @ + -`) and passwords 8\u2013256 characters.\n\nThe backend is all in `backend/app.py`, which keeps its SQLite database at `data/app.db`. The frontend is in `frontend/src/App.tsx` and `api.ts`. I added Tailwind and TypeScript to `package.json`, pinned their versions and updated the lock file. I also added an `npm run typecheck` script and wrote the configuration options into `README.md`. The `Dockerfile` didn't need changes.",
